    "show_share": true,
    "description": "The African College of Neuropsychopharmacology (AfCNP) is launching its first-ever school, an event set to transform neuropsychopharmacology research across Africa. Hosted by the Aga Khan University's Brain & Mind Institute in Nairobi, this intensive 7-day program will run from June 2-8 and focus on the neuropsychopharmacology of stress and substance use disorders. The event will bring together 21 early-career to mid-level African researchers and 10 distinguished faculty members for an immersive learning experience.",
